From: OpenWrt AX3000E port
Date: Mon Aug 24 2026
Subject: [PATCH] net: skbuff_recycle: guard active_extensions on CONFIG_SKB_EXTENSIONS

skb->active_extensions is only compiled into struct sk_buff when
CONFIG_SKB_EXTENSIONS is enabled (see include/linux/skbuff.h, which
guards every other reference to this field the same way). This
targets kernel config leaves CONFIG_SKB_EXTENSIONS off (it is a
select-only, promptless Kconfig bool with no board here selecting
it), so skbuff_recycle.h unconditional reference to the field is a
hard compile error. Guard it like upstream does everywhere else; skip
the check entirely when extensions are not compiled in, which is safe
since no skb can have any active extensions in that case.

--- a/net/core/skbuff_recycle.h
+++ b/net/core/skbuff_recycle.h
@@ -158,8 +158,10 @@
 	if (unlikely(skb_pfmemalloc(skb)))
 		return false;
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_SKB_EXTENSIONS
 	if (skb->active_extensions)
 		return false;
+#endif
 
 	return true;
 }
